# cs2gs ilverify allow-unsafe marker (gsharp issue #1933 / #1985).
#
# WinFileIO performs low-level unbuffered file I/O via raw unmanaged
# pointers/native-int arithmetic (unsafe fixed-buffer pointer code). This is
# inherently unverifiable IL -- the C# compiler emits the exact same
# unverifiable instructions for the same source -- so ilverify legitimately
# reports errors for these methods. This is expected-unverifiable, not a gsc
# emit bug. Scope the allowance to just this type so a genuine unsafe-IL
# regression elsewhere in Foundation still gates.
Oahu.Aux.Win32.WinFileIO
